module tasks.`2026-11-20-transcript-inline-images`

task TranscriptInlineImages {
  title "Inline images in harness transcripts: one off-thread image-preparation hook, fed by the existing document PNG resolver"
  verify $ cargo nextest run -p bboxy450-harness -E 'test(image)' && cargo nextest run -p bboxy450-term -E 'test(images)'
  paths "crates/bboxy450-harness", "crates/bboxy450-term/src/documents", "crates/bbt-doc", "Cargo.lock"
  brief """
    Our stand: subtract before you add; reuse before you build; no second decoder. Operator (2026-11-20): "render inline images in bboxy harness ... smallest set of changes".

    ## Design (from the approved spec text `specs/python-charts.den` "Image resolver, transcript and canvas", on `origin/handoff/nyx-svg-artifacts-20261120`)
    - Today: `bbt-doc` parses `![alt](target)` into `Inline::Image { target, alt, asset: None }` (`crates/bbt-doc/src/markdown/parse.rs:350`); layout draws `Piece::Image(asset)` only when `asset` is `Some` and otherwise prints `[image: alt] (target)` (`layout.rs:1080`). Nobody sets `asset` for transcripts.
    - Documents already resolve images: `crates/bboxy450-term/src/documents/images.rs:60-102` (flat names in `.bboxy/images`, PNG, bounded: 16 MiB encoded, each side 1..2047, <=16 distinct targets per document, <=4,000,000 decoded pixels total; symlink/escape refusals).
    - **Add one narrow host image-preparation hook** in the harness transcript path before fragment layout (`src/frontends/gui/rich.rs:549-623`, `transcript_body_element` ~602), on the existing off-thread path. The term host implements it with the **same** `images::load`; limits apply per message. Standalone harness hosts without an authorized root show the alt-text placeholder (no file probing).
    - Invalidate a prepared block when its image result changes even if the message text is unchanged (needed later for artifact updates).
    - This hook is the one Phase C extends with `artifact:ID[:N]` and SVG ([[tasks/2026-11-20-svg-renderer-artifacts]]); shape it so that branch is one match arm.

    ## Verify
    - Unit: a message with a `.bboxy/images` PNG gets an asset; missing, oversize, 17th target, symlink, path traversal -> placeholder, rest of the message intact.
    - Native GUI capture via the app's `--capture` on a private fixture account showing an inline PNG in a transcript reply.
    - `make land` (one gate machine-wide). Harness change lands through the harness first, then `make bump-harness`.
    ## Oracle amendment, 2026-11-20 18:20: term host wiring paths
    - Granted: `crates/bboxy450-term/src/rich_faces.rs` (seat-bound pane connection, :136), `crates/bboxy450-term/src/rich_pane.rs` (off-thread preparation and texture publication, :325), and `crates/bboxy450-term/tests/swarm_workdir/rich_detach.rs` for the private `--capture` witness. Keep the hook narrow: the pane passes its authorized root to the same `documents::images` resolver; no second decoder or store.

    ## Oracle amendment, 2026-11-20 19:00: headless capture path
    - Granted `crates/bboxy450-term/src/headless.rs`: the headless `--capture` (`headless.rs:522`) uploads pane snapshot textures through the existing `install_document_images`, mirroring the window path at `main.rs:8369`. Reuse that call; no headless-only image path.


    ## Report from seat:01M7XBGWB3P8Y1NQD75NPPHT6Y

    [[Done]] Native transcripts paint workspace Markdown PNGs at their natural size. The landed private capture found 6,048 probe pixels in the 96 × 64 image between two reply lines. Nine harness and seven term image tests passed. All 2,456 gallery renders and comparison rows matched the base. Removed full-column stretching and the post-decode pixel check. The signed term and harness commits are on main, with exact-source native/TLC receipts linked in the report.

    ```json
    {
      "op_id": "01M7YDX847XWDZ324D3PKSQ6BX",
      "commit": "dbc521bcec1f08939cb54bbd3f6038cff555a3de",
      "report": "[[reports/2026-11-20-transcript-inline-images.den]]",
      "verify_result": {
        "command": "cargo nextest run -p bboxy450-harness -E 'test(image)' && cargo nextest run -p bboxy450-term -E 'test(images)'",
        "exit_code": 0,
        "evidence": [
          {
            "criterion": "Harness callback, bitmap bounds and root fencing",
            "reference": "target/svg-handoff/transcript-images-harness.log"
          },
          {
            "criterion": "Term image admission",
            "reference": "target/svg-handoff/transcript-images-term-final.log"
          },
          {
            "criterion": "Native capture between text rows",
            "reference": "target/svg-handoff/transcript-images-landed-capture.log"
          },
          {
            "criterion": "Gallery differential",
            "reference": "target/svg-handoff/transcript-images-gallery-qualification.json"
          },
          {
            "criterion": "Landed native and TLC parity",
            "reference": "target/svg-handoff/transcript-images-landed-formal.log"
          }
        ]
      }
    }
    ```
    """

  managed {
    allowed_paths = json"[\"crates/bboxy450-harness\",\"crates/bboxy450-term/src/documents\",\"crates/bbt-doc\",\"Cargo.lock\",\"crates/bboxy450-term/src/rich_faces.rs\",\"crates/bboxy450-term/src/rich_pane.rs\",\"crates/bboxy450-term/tests/swarm_workdir/rich_detach.rs\",\"crates/bboxy450-term/src/headless.rs\"]"
